Some beats of this script break the rules. REWRITE ONLY the beats listed
under FIX THESE BEATS. Every other beat is final and must not change.

THE WHOLE SCRIPT, for context:
{% for b in beats %}
  beat {{ b.n }} ({{ b.role }}): {{ b.voice }}
{% endfor %}

FIX THESE BEATS:
{% for item in broken %}

beat {{ item.beat.n }} ({{ item.beat.role }}) -- now {{ item.words }} words; rewrite as a fact line of at most {{ fact_words }} words and a punch of at most {{ punch_words }}:
  now:            "{{ item.beat.voice }}"
  year_stamp:     "{{ item.beat.year_stamp }}"
  on_screen_text: "{{ item.beat.on_screen_text }}"
  ref_ids:        {{ item.beat.ref_ids }}
  what is wrong:
{% for v in item.violations %}
    - {{ v.message }}
{% endfor %}
{% if item.facts %}
  the facts it cites -- the ONLY source for any number in this beat:
{% for f in item.facts %}
    {{ f.id }} [{{ f.label }}]: {{ f.claim }}
        quote: "{{ f.evidence }}"
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if item.references %}
  the ONLY comparisons this beat may mention (list the id in ref_ids if you do):
{% for r in item.references %}
    {{ r.id }} {{ r.reference }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
  this beat may mention NO modern comparison or brand at all.
{% endif %}
{% if item.echo_words %}
  reuse at least {{ loop_words }} of these words from beat 1, so the video loops: {{ item.echo_words|join(", ") }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

Keep each beat's meaning: say LESS, not something else. Numbers as digits,
only ones in that beat's cited facts. The last beat must reuse key words from
beat 1 so the video loops.

Return JSON: {"beats": [...]} with one object per beat listed above, each with
"n", "fact_line" and "punch", plus "on_screen_text" and "ref_ids" if they
change. The fact line copies the fact's date exactly as its label writes it.
